-- title:
--   Change of floor X₀(qM')→ X₀(M') unramified at an ordinary point
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $L$ a field of characteristic zero, algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$, and such that some ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb{C}$ carries $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ over $L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_H(q^2M')$, where $H\le(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ is the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $q$ and $\zeta$ lie in $A$ respectively in its maximal ideal and its image, with uniformiser $\varpi$, and let $j\in K$ be the element whose Laurent series is the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant, $j\neq0$. Let $W_0$ be the valuation subring of $K$ consisting of the $f$ with $f\cdot y=x$ for power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction. On the two-chart integral model over $A$ attached to $K$ and $j$ — the pushout of the spectra of the algebras $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}$, $\mathrm{chartAlgInf}$ of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, resp. $A[j^{-1}]$ — let $z$ be a point at which the germ of $\varpi$ (pulled back along the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec}A$) lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and let $y\in\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j)$ be a point above $z$ whose prime $y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ is maximal. Assume: there is a ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ to an algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ with kernel $y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ such that $\varphi(j)$ does not lie in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$, i.e. $\varphi(j)$ is the invariant of some elliptic curve over $\Omega$ possessing a nonzero $q$-torsion point; and every element of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ that is a nonunit of $W_0$ lies in $y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$. Let further $K_0\le K_0'\le K$ be the $L$-base changes of the $q$-expansion function fields of $\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\Gamma_0(qM')$, with elements $j_0,j_0'$ again given by the $q$-expansion of $j$ and nonzero, let $\iota_0'$, $\iota'$, $\iota$ be ring homomorphisms between the corresponding finite-chart algebras compatible with the field inclusions and satisfying $\iota=\iota'\circ\iota_0'$, and assume the structure morphism of the two-chart integral model of $(K_0,j_0)$ over $\operatorname{Spec}A$ is smooth. Then, with $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K_0'\,j_0'$ viewed as an algebra over $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K_0\,j_0$ via $\iota_0'$, this algebra is unramified at the prime $\iota'^{-1}(y.\mathrm{asIdeal})$, that is, the localisation there is formally unramified over $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K_0\,j_0$.
--
--   This is the change-of-floor step for the integral models: at a closed point of the special fibre lying on the component cut out by the Gauss valuation $W_0$ and having ordinary $j$-invariant, the degeneracy map $X_0(qM')\to X_0(M')$ is unramified at the induced prime. It feeds the regularity statement for the special fibre of the model of $X_H(q^2M')$, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.isRegularLocalRing_fibre_of_forall_height_one_isUnramifiedAt_off_section_xH_of_isSeparable`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.isRegularLocalRing_fibre_of_forall_height_one_isUnramifiedAt_off_section_xH_of_isSeparable).
